# p5 mcp discover: four stdio servers whose discover answer nests `supportedVersions` 126,
# 2582, 2583 and 4000 arrays deep (p5-mcp-discover-stdio.ts `deep:<n>`), inside the line's
# object and its result: 128, 2584, 2585 and 4002 levels in all. fx v0.0.16's decoder reads
# a line nested as deep as its scanner's stack allows (`scan_stack_bytes`,
# src/mcp/protocol/wire.zig:100-101@481104fd) -- 2584 levels, found by these captures: such
# an answer lists no version (retrying); a deeper line is no answer at all, so its probe
# waits out its 10 s and `initialize` follows (ready). `/mcp list` at 16 s.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-depth-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-discover-stdio-depth-profile.json
gateway p5-mcp-hello.json
wait 16
type /mcp list
key Enter
wait 2
snap list
